{"ts": "2026-08-17T13:15:39Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 171, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\t# Design: Let me undo deleting a task\n2\t\n3\t**Taiga:** #13\n4\t**Spec:** `docs/spec.md`\n5\t\n6\t## Summary of the interaction\n7\t\n8\tDeleting a task no longer needs a confirmation dialog \u2014 the ticket asks for\n9\tforgiveness, not permission. The row disappears immediately (per spec, this\n10\tis `App.jsx` filtering it out of `tasks`, not mutating it) and a small\n11\tnotice appears at the bottom of the viewport with the task's title and an\n12\tUndo button. The notice disappears on its own after 5 seconds, or on click.\n13\t\n14\t## Components: reused vs. new\n15\t\n16\t- **New:** `frontend/src/components/UndoToast.jsx` \u2014 one row per pending\n17\t  delete, per the spec's affected-areas note.\n18\t- **Reused as-is, no changes:** `.task`/`.task-list` row styling for the\n19\t  restored row (nothing to design \u2014 the row just re-enters the existing\n20\t  list unchanged, including `.task.done`'s strikethrough for AC4).\n21\t- **No new UI library, icon set, or token system.** The rest of the app is\n22\t  plain CSS with no icon usage anywhere (checked `TaskList.jsx`,\n23\t  `ClearCompleted.jsx`, `TaskCounts.jsx`, `TaskFilter.jsx` \u2014 the only\n24\t  \"icon\" in the app is the inline `\u26a0` glyph on `.overdue-badge`). This\n25\t  design follows suit: text only, no icon.\n26\t\n27\t## Data shape into the component\n28\t\n29\t`App.jsx` already holds full task objects in `tasks` (untouched during the\n30\tundo window, per spec). `UndoToast` doesn't need its own title snapshot \u2014\n31\trender it as:\n32\t\n33\t```jsx\n34\t<UndoToast\n35\t  pending={pendingDeleteIds.map((id) => tasks.find((t) => t.id === id))}\n36\t  onUndo={cancelPendingDelete}\n37\t/>\n38\t```\n39\t\n40\ti.e. `pending` is an array of full task objects (oldest pending-delete\n41\tfirst, matching insertion order \u2014 no reordering logic needed). `UndoToast`\n42\tonly reads `.id` and `.title` off each.\n43\t\n44\t## Placement in the tree and DOM\n45\t\n46\tMount `<UndoToast>` as the last child of `<main className=\"app\">` in\n47\t`App.jsx`, after `<TaskList>` (unconditionally \u2014 not gated behind\n48\t`!loading`, since a pending delete can only exist once tasks have loaded).\n49\tIt's positioned with `position: fixed`, so DOM order doesn't affect visual\n50\tplacement, but it does fix tab order: keyboard users reach the Undo\n51\tbutton(s) *last*, after all task-row controls. That's an accepted\n52\tconsequence, not a gap to design around \u2014 see \"Focus\" below.\n53\t\n54\t## States\n55\t\n56\t### Empty (no pending deletes)\n57\t\n58\t`UndoToast` returns `null`. Nothing is rendered \u2014 no empty container sits\n59\tin the DOM, matching the fact that there's nothing to announce.\n60\t\n61\t### Populated \u2014 one pending delete\n62\t\n63\t```\n64\t                    (rest of the page, unaffected)\n65\t\n66\t              \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n67\t              \u2502  \"Buy groceries\" deleted           Undo  \u2502\n68\t              \u2502  \u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591  \u2502\n69\t              \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n70\t                    fixed, bottom-center, above content\n71\t```\n72\t\n73\tThe bottom bar is a decorative, `aria-hidden` progress track that shrinks\n74\tfrom 100% to 0% width over 5s (pure CSS `@keyframes`, `animation-duration`\n75\tset inline from the same 5000ms constant `App.jsx` uses for the timeout \u2014\n76\tone source of truth, no drift between the visual and the real timer).\n77\t\n78\t### Populated \u2014 many (AC5: two+ independent pending deletes)\n79\t\n80\tStacked in a column, oldest on top, each with its own independent bar:\n81\t\n82\t```\n83\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n84\t\u2502  \"Buy groceries\" deleted           Undo  \u2502\n85\t\u2502  \u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591  \u2502\n86\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n87\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n88\t\u2502  \"Call dentist\" deleted            Undo  \u2502\n89\t\u2502  \u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591  \u2502\n90\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n91\t```\n92\t\n93\tEach row's bar is driven by its own `animationDuration`/mount time \u2014 one\n94\tundoing does not affect another's remaining time (AC5).\n95\t\n96\t### Populated \u2014 long title\n97\t\n98\tTitle truncates with an ellipsis rather than wrapping or pushing the Undo\n99\tbutton off-row (title + button must stay one row, per spec):\n100\t\n101\t```\n102\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n103\t\u2502  \"Migrate the entire billing sys\u2026  Undo  \u2502\n104\t\u2502  \u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2593\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591\u2591  \u2502\n105\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n106\t```\n107\t\n108\tCSS: `overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap;` on\n109\tthe title span, plus a `title=\"{task.title}\"` attribute so the full text\n110\tis available on hover as a native tooltip. Undo button has `flex-shrink: 0`\n111\tso it's never the thing that gets squeezed.\n112\t\n113\t### Interactive\n114\t\n115\t- **Undo button, default:** transparent background, `1px solid` light\n116\t  border, white text (see contrast computation below).\n117\t- **Undo button, hover:** `background: rgba(255,255,255,0.12)`.\n118\t- **Undo button, active/pressed:** `background: rgba(255,255,255,0.2)`.\n119\t- **Undo button, focus-visible:** explicit `outline: 2px solid #ffffff;\n120\t  outline-offset: 2px;`. The rest of the app has no focus styling anywhere\n121\t  (checked \u2014 no `:focus` rule exists in `App.css`), so it relies on the\n122\t  browser default outline, which is typically a blue ring; on this new\n123\t  dark (`#16191c`) background a blue ring's contrast isn't guaranteed\n124\t  across browsers, so this component defines its own to be sure the\n125\t  3:1 non-text contrast minimum actually holds (see below).\n126\t- **Row removed:** whether by Undo click or by the 5s window elapsing, the\n127\t  row (and its pending-delete entry) is removed together \u2014 there is no\n128\t  disabled/stale intermediate state, per the spec's \"no stale button\"\n129\t  edge case.\n130\t\n131\t### Loading / Error\n132\t\n133\tNeither applies to this component. Undo is a synchronous local state\n134\tchange (cancel a timeout, un-filter an id) \u2014 no network call, so no\n135\tin-flight state. The one failure mode that *can* happen (the deferred\n136\t`DELETE` 404s because the task was already removed some other way) is\n137\tswallowed silently per AC6 \u2014 no design element represents it, by design,\n138\tthe same way `.empty`'s edge cases are silently accepted elsewhere in this\n139\tapp. If the deferred `DELETE` fails for a *different* reason (network\n140\terror, 5xx \u2014 not covered by an AC), it should surface through the existing\n141\ttop-of-page `<p className=\"error\" role=\"alert\">` banner in `App.jsx:65`,\n142\texactly like every other mutation in this app (`run()`'s `catch` block) \u2014\n143\tno new error UI, reusing what's already there.\n144\t\n145\t## Styling decisions\n146\t\n147\t| Element | Value | Reasoning |\n148\t|---|---|---|\n149\t| Toast background | `#16191c` | Already used in this codebase as an \"inverted\" surface (`.filter-option.active`, `App.css:75`) \u2014 reusing it rather than inventing a new dark tone. |\n150\t| Toast text (title) | `#ffffff` | Paired with the above. |\n151\t| Toast row padding/radius | `0.6rem 0.8rem` / `6px` | Matches `.task`'s existing row treatment (`App.css:28`) so the toast reads as \"the same kind of row, recolored,\" not a new shape language. |\n152\t| Row gap (stacked toasts) | `0.5rem` | Matches `.task-list`'s existing `gap: 0.5rem` (`App.css:25`). |\n153\t| Row-internal gap (title/button) | `0.5rem` | Matches `.task`'s internal `gap: 0.5rem`. |\n154\t| Undo button border | `rgba(255,255,255,0.55)` | See contrast computation below. |\n155\t| Bottom offset | `1.2rem` | Matches the existing spacing scale's largest step (`margin-bottom: 1.2rem` used twice in `App.css`). |\n156\t| Width | `width: calc(100% - 2rem); max-width: 26rem;` centered via `left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%);` | The app has no breakpoints today (no `@media` anywhere in `App.css`) and no fixed-position precedent; this keeps the toast readable and centered from narrow phones up through the `.app` container's own `34rem` cap, without introducing a breakpoint system. |\n157\t| `z-index` | `10` | Nothing else in the app sets `z-index`; this is the first fixed/overlaid element, so any value above the default stacking order works \u2014 picked `10` with room to spare rather than `1`. |\n158\t| Progress bar track / fill | `rgba(255,255,255,0.18)` / `rgba(255,255,255,0.65)` | Decorative only (`aria-hidden=\"true\"`), so no contrast minimum applies \u2014 values chosen just for visible-but-not-competing-with-text. |\n159\t\n160\t## Accessibility\n161\t\n162\t**Contrast \u2014 text.** Title text `#ffffff` on toast background `#16191c`:\n163\trelative luminance of `#16191c` \u2248 0.0095, white = 1.0 \u2192\n164\t**contrast ratio \u2248 17.6:1** (needs 4.5:1 for normal text \u2014 passes with\n165\tlarge margin, same pairing already in use elsewhere in this codebase).\n166\t\n167\t**Contrast \u2014 non-text (button border).** Border `rgba(255,255,255,0.55)`\n168\tcomposited over `#16191c` \u2248 `rgb(150,152,153)`. Luminance \u2248 0.312 vs.\n169\tbackground's 0.0095 \u2192 **contrast ratio \u2248 6.1:1** (needs 3:1 for non-text UI\n170\tcomponents \u2014 passes).\n171\t\n172\t**Contrast \u2014 focus outline.** `#ffffff` outline on `#16191c` background is\n173\tthe same pairing as the title text \u2192 **\u224817.6:1**, passes.\n174\t\n175\t**Target size.** The Undo button uses the same base `button` sizing as\n176\tevery other button in this app (`padding: 0.5rem 0.8rem`, `App.css:16-22`)\n177\t\u2014 roughly 34\u201336px tall at the default font size, below the 44px\n178\trecommendation. This is consistent with every existing button in the app\n179\t(Edit/Done/Delete/Save/Cancel all share this sizing), so introducing a\n180\tlarger target *only* for Undo would make it visually inconsistent with its\n181\tneighbors for a gap that predates this feature. Not fixed here \u2014 flagging\n182\tit as a pre-existing, app-wide condition, not something new this feature\n183\tintroduces.\n184\t\n185\t**Focus.** The toast does **not** programmatically steal focus when it\n186\tappears. Standard toast/snackbar guidance is not to move focus\n187\tautomatically (it's disruptive mid-task for keyboard/screen-reader users),\n188\tand nothing else in this app moves focus after a mutation today (Add,\n189\tComplete, and Delete itself all leave focus wherever it was). Combined\n190\twith the spec's non-goal of no keyboard shortcut, keyboard-only users reach\n191\tUndo by tabbing to it in DOM order (last, after all task rows) within the\n192\t5s window, or they don't \u2014 that's an accepted limitation of \"click only,\"\n193\tnot something this design compensates for.\n194\t\n195\t**Live region.** Container `<div className=\"undo-toast-list\" role=\"status\">`\n196\taround the row(s) \u2014 `role=\"status\"` implies `aria-live=\"polite\"` and\n197\tmatches `TaskCounts.jsx`'s existing choice (`role=\"status\"`, `App.jsx`\n198\tpattern for non-urgent, appearing/updating status text) rather than\n199\t`.error`'s `role=\"alert\"` (reserved for the urgent/blocking case). Each\n200\tindividual row does not need its own live region \u2014 the container\n201\tannounces new rows as they're added; row *removal* (undo or expiry) is not\n202\tseparately announced, which is standard and fine (nothing in the ACs\n203\trequires the disappearance itself to be announced).\n204\t\n205\t## Traceability to acceptance criteria\n206\t\n207\t| AC | Design element |\n208\t|---|---|\n209\t| 1 (row disappears, notice shows title + Undo) | \"Populated \u2014 one pending delete\" state |\n210\t| 2 (Undo restores exact row) | \"Interactive\" Undo button behavior; restored row reuses unmodified `.task` styling \u2014 nothing to reconstruct visually |\n211\t| 3 (5s elapses \u2192 notice disappears on its own) | Progress bar's `animation-duration` shares App.jsx's timeout constant; row removal on expiry, same as Undo removal |\n212\t| 4 (done task stays done after undo) | No new visual state needed \u2014 `.task.done`'s existing strikethrough (`App.css:31`) applies automatically since the task object was never mutated |\n213\t| 5 (two independent pending deletes) | \"Populated \u2014 many\" stacked state, independent per-row bars |\n214\t| 6 (404 on expiry is silent) | Explicitly no design element \u2014 covered under \"Loading / Error\" above |\n215\t\n216\t## Open items carried from the spec\n217\t\n218\tNone beyond the spec's own open question (5s duration), which is a\n219\tbehavioral constant, not a design decision \u2014 the progress bar's animation\n220\tlength simply mirrors whatever `App.jsx` uses.\n221\t", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_016Gx8qNE3rcWjcaVJ96pv98", "session_id": "efe54001-69c6-45a9-9728-9e9432a09ec4"}}
